es", "d": null, "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000321105821", "dep": null}, {"v": "99", "n": "Other", "d": null, "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000321105822", "dep": null}, {"v": "17", "n": "Behavioral health", "d": null, "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000321106136", "dep": null}, {"v": "18", "n": "Transportation", "d": null, "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000321106137", "dep": null}, {"v": "98", "n": "None", "d": null, "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000321106138", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('FinancialAccountBalanceSheetCode', 'Balance sheet accounts and statement of net position accounts are used to track financial transactions for each fund. Such financial statements only report assets, deferred outflows of resources, liabilities, deferred inflows of resources, and equity accounts and are considered "snapshots" of how these accounts stand as of a certain point in time.', NULL, 'scheme: C001353', NULL, $j$[{"v": "101", "n": "Cash in Bank", "d": "All funds on deposit with a bank or savings and loan institution, normally in non-interest-bearing accounts. Interest-bearing accounts, however, that do not meet the definition of an investment (e.g., demand deposits that are interest-bearing) should be recorded herein as well.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117332", "dep": null}, {"v": "102", "n": "Cash on Hand", "d": "Currency, coins, checks, postal and express money orders, and bankers' drafts on hand.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117333", "dep": null}, {"v": "103", "n": "Petty Cash", "d": "A sum of money set aside to pay small obligations for which the issuance of a formal voucher and check would be too expensive and time consuming.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117334", "dep": null}, {"v": "104", "n": "Change Cash", "d": "A sum of money set aside to provide change.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117335", "dep": null}, {"v": "105", "n": "Cash With Fiscal Agents", "d": "Deposits with fiscal agents, such as commercial banks, for paying matured bonds and interest.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117336", "dep": null}, {"v": "111", "n": "Investments", "d": "Securities and real estate held for producing income in the form of interest, dividends, rentals, or lease payments. Investments should be presented at fair value as of the reporting date. Gains from changes in the fair value of investments are recorded using revenue account 1530. Losses from changes in the fair value of investments are recorded using expenditure object code 930. Alternatively, gains and losses may be netted and recorded in revenue account 1530. The account does not include capital assets used in school district operations. Separate accounts may be maintained for each category of investments.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117337", "dep": null}, {"v": "112", "n": "Unamortized Premiums on Investments", "d": "The excess of the amount paid for securities over the face value that has not yet been amortized. Use of this account is restricted to short- term money market investments.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117338", "dep": null}, {"v": "113", "n": "Unamortized Discounts on Investments (Credit)", "d": "The excess of the face value of securities over the amount paid for them that has not yet been written off. Use of this account is restricted to short-term investments.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117339", "dep": null}, {"v": "114", "n": "Interest Receivable on Investments", "d": "The amount of interest receivable on investments, excluding interest purchased. Interest purchased should be shown in a separate account.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117340", "dep": null}, {"v": "115", "n": "Accrued Interest on Investments Purchased", "d": "Interest accrued on investments between the last interest payment date and the date of purchase. The account is carried as an asset until the first interest payment date after the date of purchase.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117341", "dep": null}, {"v": "121", "n": "Taxes Receivable", "d": "The uncollected portion of taxes that a school district or government unit has levied and that has become due, including any interest or penalties that may be accrued. Separate accounts may be maintained on the basis of tax roll year, current and delinquent taxes, or both.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117342", "dep": null}, {"v": "122", "n": "Allowance for Uncollectible Taxes (Credit)", "d": "The portion of taxes receivable estimated not to be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the taxes receivable account to arrive at the net taxes receivable. Separate accounts may be maintained on the basis of tax roll year, delinquent taxes, or both.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117343", "dep": null}, {"v": "131", "n": "Interfund Loans Receivable", "d": "An asset account used to record a loan by one fund to another fund in the same governmental unit. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interfund receivable loan.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117344", "dep": null}, {"v": "132", "n": "Interfund Accounts Receivable", "d": "An asset account used to indicate amounts owed to a particular fund by another fund in the same school district for goods sold or services rendered. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interfund receivable.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117345", "dep": null}, {"v": "141", "n": "Intergovernmental Accounts Receivable", "d": "Amounts due to the reporting governmental unit from another governmental unit. These amounts may represent grants-in-aid, shared taxes, taxes collected for the reporting unit by another unit, loans, and charges for services rendered by the reporting unit for another government. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interagency receivable.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117346", "dep": null}, {"v": "151", "n": "Loans Receivable", "d": "Amounts that have been loaned to persons or organizations, including notes taken as security for such loans, where permitted by statutory authority.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117347", "dep": null}, {"v": "152", "n": "Allowance for Uncollectible Loans (Credit)", "d": "The portion of loans receivable estimated not to be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the other loans receivable account.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117348", "dep": null}, {"v": "153", "n": "Other Accounts Receivable", "d": "Amounts due on open account from private persons, firms, or corporations for goods and services furnished by a school district (but not including amounts due from other funds or from other governmental units).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117349", "dep": null}, {"v": "154", "n": "Allowance for Uncollectible Accounts Receivable (Credit)", "d": "A provision for that portion of accounts receivable that is estimated will not be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the other accounts receivable account.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117350", "dep": null}, {"v": "171", "n": "Inventories for Consumption", "d": "The cost of supplies and equipment on hand not yet distributed to requisitioning units.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117351", "dep": null}, {"v": "172", "n": "Inventories for Resale", "d": "The value of goods purchased and held by a school district for resale rather than for use in its own operations. Such goods could include unique manufactured inventories, such as student-built homes or equipment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117352", "dep": null}, {"v": "181", "n": "Prepaid Items", "d": "Expenditures/expenses paid for benefits not yet received. Prepaid expenses differ from deferred charges in that they are spread over a shorter period of time and are regularly recurring costs of operation. Examples of prepaid expenses are prepaid rent, prepaid interest, and unexpired insurance premiums.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117353", "dep": null}, {"v": "191", "n": "Deposits", "d": "Funds deposited by the school district as a prerequisite to receiving services, goods, or both.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117354", "dep": null}, {"v": "193", "n": "Bond Insurance Costs", "d": "Bond insurance costs that are a form of prepayment to be amortized.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117355", "dep": null}, {"v": "194", "n": "Premium and Discount on Issuance of Bonds", "d": "Represents amounts to be amortized as debt premium/discount in connection with the issuance of bonds.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117356", "dep": null}, {"v": "199", "n": "Other Current Assets", "d": "Current assets not provided for elsewhere.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117357", "dep": null}, {"v": "200", "n": "Capital Assets", "d": "Those assets that the school district intends to hold or continue to use over a long period of time. Specifically, capital assets include land, improvements to land, easements, buildings and building improvements, vehicles, machinery, equipment, works of art and historical treasures, infrastructure, and all other tangible or intangible assets that are used in operations and that have initial useful lives that extend beyond a single reporting period. This account is used only in proprietary funds, fiduciary funds, and the government-wide financial statements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117358", "dep": null}, {"v": "241", "n": "Machinery and Equipment", "d": "Tangible property of a more or less permanent nature, other than land, buildings, or improvements thereto, that is useful in carrying on operations. Examples are machinery, tools, trucks, cars, buses, computers, purchased software, furniture, and furnishings. Appendix E provides criteria to distinguish whether a purchase is a supply or a piece of machinery or equipment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117364", "dep": null}, {"v": "211", "n": "Land and Land Improvements", "d": "A capital asset account that reflects the acquisition value of land owned by a school district. If land is purchased, this account includes the purchase price and costs such as legal fees, filling and excavation costs, and other associated improvement costs incurred to put the land in condition for its intended use. If land is acquired by gift, the account reflects its fair value at the time of acquisition. Permanent improvements to land, such as grading and fill, should also be accounted for in this account. Land and land improvements are considered nonexhaustible assets owing to their significantly long expected useful life. Nonexhaustible assets are not to be depreciated. Therefore, assets classified by asset code 211 should result in no depreciation expense.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117359", "dep": null}, {"v": "221", "n": "Site Improvements", "d": "A capital asset account that reflects the value of nonpermanent improvements to building sites, other than buildings, that add value to land. Examples of such improvements are fences, retaining walls, sidewalks, pavements, gutters, tunnels, and bridges. If the improvements are purchased or constructed, this account contains the purchase or contract price. If improvements are obtained by gift, it reflects the fair value at the time of acquisition. Site improvements are improvements that have a limited useful life. Because these improvements decrease in their value/usefulness over time, it is appropriate to depreciate these assets. Therefore, all capitalized site improvements should be depreciated over their expected useful life.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117360", "dep": null}, {"v": "222", "n": "Accumulated Depreciation on Site Improvements", "d": "Accumulated amounts for the depreciation of land improvements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117361", "dep": null}, {"v": "231", "n": "Buildings and Building Improvements", "d": "A capital asset account that reflects the acquisition value of permanent structures used to house persons and property owned by the school district. If buildings are purchased or constructed, this account includes the purchase or contract price of all permanent buildings and the fixtures attached to and forming a permanent part of such buildings. This account includes all building improvements, including upgrades made to building wiring for technology. If buildings are acquired by gift, the account reflects their fair value at the time of acquisition.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117362", "dep": null}, {"v": "232", "n": "Accumulated Depreciation on Buildings and Building Improvements", "d": "Accumulated amounts for the depreciation of buildings and building improvements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117363", "dep": null}, {"v": "242", "n": "Accumulated Depreciation on Machinery and Equipment", "d": "Accumulated amounts for the depreciation of machinery and equipment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117365", "dep": null}, {"v": "251", "n": "Works of Art and Historical Treasures", "d": "Individual items or collections of items that are of artistic or cultural importance.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117366", "dep": null}, {"v": "252", "n": "Accumulated Depreciation on Works of Art and Historical Collections", "d": "Accumulated amounts for the depreciation (as applicable) of works of art and historical treasures.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117367", "dep": null}, {"v": "261", "n": "Infrastructure", "d": "A capital asset, network, or subsystem that has a useful life that is significantly longer than those of other capital assets. These assets may include water/sewer systems, roads, bridges, tunnels, and other similar assets.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117368", "dep": null}, {"v": "262", "n": "Accumulated Depreciation on Infrastructure", "d": "Accumulated amounts for the depreciation of infrastructure assets.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117369", "dep": null}, {"v": "271", "n": "Construction in Progress", "d": "The cost of construction work undertaken but not yet completed.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117370", "dep": null}, {"v": "281", "n": "Intangible Assets", "d": "An intangible asset is a capital asset that lacks physical substance, is nonfinancial in nature, and has an initial useful life of more than 1 year. Intangible assets may be purchased or licensed, acquired through nonexchange transactions, or internally generated. Examples include easements, contractual rights, patents, trademarks, and computer software.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117371", "dep": null}, {"v": "282", "n": "Accumulated Amortization of Intangible Assets", "d": "Accumulated amounts for the amortization of intangible assets.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117372", "dep": null}, {"v": "300", "n": "Deferred Outflows of Resources", "d": "A consumption of net assets by the government that is applicable to a future reporting period.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117373", "dep": null}, {"v": "401", "n": "Interfund Loans Payable", "d": "A liability account used to record a debt owed by one fund to another fund in the same governmental unit. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interfund loan.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117374", "dep": null}, {"v": "402", "n": "Interfund Accounts Payable", "d": "A liability account used to indicate amounts owed by a particular fund for services rendered. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interfund payable.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117375", "dep": null}, {"v": "411", "n": "Intergovernmental Accounts Payable", "d": "Amounts owed by the reporting school district to another governmental unit. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each intergovernmental payable.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117376", "dep": null}, {"v": "421", "n": "Accounts Payable", "d": "Liabilities on open account owed to private persons, firms, or corporations for goods and services received by a school district (but not including amounts due to other funds of the same school district or to other governmental units).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117377", "dep": null}, {"v": "422", "n": "Judgments Payable", "d": "Amounts due to be paid by a school district as the result of court decisions, including condemnation awards paid for private property taken for public use.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117378", "dep": null}, {"v": "423", "n": "Warrants Payable", "d": "Amounts due to designated payees in the form of a written order drawn by the school district directing the school district treasurer to pay a specific amount.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117379", "dep": null}, {"v": "431", "n": "Contracts Payable", "d": "Amounts due on contracts for assets, goods, and services received by a school district.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117380", "dep": null}, {"v": "432", "n": "Construction Contracts Payable-Retainage", "d": "Liabilities on account of construction contracts for that portion of the work that has been completed but on which part the liability has not been paid pending final inspection, the lapse of a specified time period, or both. The unpaid amount is usually a stated percentage of the contract price.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117381", "dep": null}, {"v": "433", "n": "Construction Contracts Payable", "d": "Amounts due by a school district on contracts for constructing buildings and other structures and other improvements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117382", "dep": null}, {"v": "441", "n": "Matured Bonds Payable", "d": "Bonds that have reached or passed their maturity date but that remain unpaid.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117383", "dep": null}, {"v": "442", "n": "Bonds Payable-Current", "d": "Bonds that have not reached or passed their maturity date but are due within 1 year or less. This account is used only in proprietary or fiduciary funds, as well as in the government-wide financial statements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117384", "dep": null}, {"v": "443", "n": "Unamortized Premiums on Issuance of Bonds", "d": "An account that represents that portion of the excess of bond proceeds over par value and that remains to be amortized over the remaining life of such bonds. This account is used only in proprietary or fiduciary funds, as well as in the government-wide financial statements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117385", "dep": null}, {"v": "451", "n": "Loans Payable (451)", "d": "Short-term obligations representing amounts borrowed for short periods of time, usually evidenced by notes payable or warrants payable.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117386\nprefLabel: Loans Payable", "dep": null}, {"v": "452", "n": "Lease Obligations-Current", "d": "Capital lease obligations that are due within 1 year.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117387", "dep": null}, {"v": "455", "n": "Interest Payable", "d": "Interest due within 1 year.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117388", "dep": null}, {"v": "461", "n": "Accrued Salaries and Benefits", "d": "Salary and fringe benefit costs incurred during the current accounting period that are not payable until a subsequent accounting period.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117389", "dep": null}, {"v": "471", "n": "Payroll Deductions and Withholdings", "d": "Amounts deducted from employees' salaries for withholding taxes and other purposes. District-paid benefits amounts payable are also included. A separate liability account may be used for each type of benefit.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117390", "dep": null}, {"v": "472", "n": "Compensated Absences-Current", "d": "Compensated absences that will be paid within 1 year.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117391", "dep": null}, {"v": "473", "n": "Accrued Annual Requirement Contribution Liability", "d": "A liability arising from payments not made to pension funds. This amount represents any difference between the actuarially determined annual required contribution and actual payments made to the pension fund.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117392", "dep": null}, {"v": "481", "n": "Advances from Grantors", "d": "A liability account that represents resources received from grantors before eligibility requirements are met.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117393", "dep": null}, {"v": "491", "n": "Deposits Payable", "d": "Liability for deposits received as a prerequisite to providing or receiving services, goods, or both.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117394", "dep": null}, {"v": "499", "n": "Other Current Liabilities", "d": "Other current liabilities not provided for elsewhere.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117395", "dep": null}, {"v": "500", "n": "Long-Term Liabilities", "d": "Obligations with a maturity of more than 1 year. These accounts should be used only with proprietary and fiduciary funds, as well as at the entity-wide level of reporting.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117396", "dep": null}, {"v": "511", "n": "Bonds Payable", "d": "Bonds (general obligation, asset-backed, or revenue-backed) that have not reached or passed their maturity date and that are not due within 1 year.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117397", "dep": null}, {"v": "512", "n": "Accreted Interest", "d": "An account that represents interest that is accrued on deep discount bonds. This account should be used by school districts that issue capital appreciation bonds. Such bonds are usually issued at a deep discount from the face value, and no interest payment is made until maturity. Under full accrual accounting, the district is required to accrete the interest on the bonds over the life of the bonds. Accretion is the process of systematically increasing the carrying amount of the bond to its estimated value at the maturity date of the bond. To calculate accreted interest, the district should impute the effective interest rate, using the present value, the face value (or the future value), and the period of the bond, and multiply the effective interest rate by the book value of the debt at the end of the period. Accreted interest is usually recorded as an addition to the outstanding debt liability.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117398", "dep": null}, {"v": "513", "n": "Unamortized Gains/Losses on Debt Refundings", "d": "An account that represents the difference between the reacquisition price and the net carrying amount of old debt when a current or advance refunding of debt occurs. This account should be used only when defeasance of debt occurs for proprietary funds and entity-wide statements. The unamortized loss amount should be reported as a deferred outflow of resources and amortized as a component of interest expense in a systematic and rational manner over the remaining life of the old debt or the life of the new debt, whichever is shorter. The unamortized gain amount should be reported as a deferred inflow of resources and amortized as a component of interest expense in a systematic and rational manner over the remaining life of the old debt or the life of the new debt, whichever is shorter.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117399", "dep": null}, {"v": "521", "n": "Loans Payable (521)", "d": "An unconditional written promise signed by the maker to pay a certain sum of money 1 year or more after the issuance date.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117400\nprefLabel: Loans Payable", "dep": null}, {"v": "531", "n": "Capital Lease Obligations", "d": "Amounts remaining to be paid on capital lease agreements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117401", "dep": null}, {"v": "551", "n": "Compensated Absences", "d": "Amounts remaining beyond the period of 1 year to be paid on compensated absences balances.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117402", "dep": null}, {"v": "553", "n": "Special Termination Benefits", "d": "These are benefits offered for a short period of time to employees in connection with their termination of employment. Special termination benefits are often used as an inducement for early retirement or to address budgetary problems.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117403", "dep": null}, {"v": "561", "n": "Arbitrage Rebate Liability", "d": "Liabilities arising from arbitrage rebates to the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) from bond financing.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117404", "dep": null}, {"v": "590", "n": "Other Long-Term Liabilities", "d": "Other long-term liabilities not provided for elsewhere. This account represents amounts due after more than 1 year from the balance sheet date for advances from other funds and certain miscellaneous liabilities, including workers' compensation, self-funded insurance, special termination benefits, and legal claims and judgments.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117405", "dep": null}, {"v": "600", "n": "Deferred Inflows of Resources", "d": "An acquisition of net assets by the government that is applicable to a future reporting period. A deferred inflow of resources should be recognized when resources are received or recognized as a receivable before (a) the period for which property taxes are levied or (b) the period when the resources are required to be used. When an asset is recorded in governmental fund financial statements but the revenue is not available, the government should report a deferred inflow of resources until such time as the revenue becomes available.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117406", "dep": null}, {"v": "710", "n": "Nonspendable Fund Balance", "d": "The nonspendable fund balance classification includes amounts that cannot be spent because they are either (a) not in spendable form or (b) legally or contractually required to be maintained intact. This would include items not expected to be converted to cash, including inventories and prepaid amounts. It may also include the long-term amount of loans and receivables, as well as property acquired for resale and the corpus (principal) of a permanent fund.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117407", "dep": null}, {"v": "720", "n": "Restricted Fund Balance", "d": "The restricted fund balance classification should be reported when legally enforceable constraints placed on the use of resources are either (a) externally imposed by creditors, grantors, contributors, or laws or regulations of other governments or (b) imposed by law through constitutional provisions or enabling legislation.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117408", "dep": null}, {"v": "730", "n": "Committed Fund Balance", "d": "The committed fund balance classification reflects specific purposes pursuant to constraints imposed by formal action at the district's highest level of decisionmaking authority (generally the governing board). Such constraints can only be removed or changed by the same form of formal action.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117409", "dep": null}, {"v": "740", "n": "Assigned Fund Balance", "d": "The assigned fund balance classification reflects amounts that are constrained by the government's intent to be used for specific purposes, but meet neither the restricted nor committed forms of constraint. Also, the assigned fund balance classification is the residual classification for the special revenue, debt service, capital projects, and/or permanent funds after nonspendable, restricted, and committed balances have been identified (unless the residual amount is negative, which would require presentation as unassigned fund balance).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117410", "dep": null}, {"v": "750", "n": "Unassigned Fund Balance", "d": "The unassigned fund balance classification is the residual classification, for the general fund only, after nonspendable, restricted, committed, and assigned balances have been identified. It is also used to report the residual amount for all other governmental funds after nonspendable, restricted, and committed balances have been identified, if the residual amount is negative.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117411", "dep": null}, {"v": "760", "n": "Net Investment in Capital Assets", "d": "This account is used to record the component of net position invested in capital assets, net of related debt, that represents total capital assets less accumulated depreciation less debt directly related to capital assets. This account is to be used only in proprietary funds and entity-wide statements. (This was previously fund balance code 740.)", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117412", "dep": null}, {"v": "770", "n": "Restricted Net Position", "d": "This account is used to record the component of net position that represents net assets legally restricted by sources internal or external to the organization. This account is to be used only in proprietary funds and entity-wide statements. (This was previously fund balance code 750.)", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117413", "dep": null}, {"v": "780", "n": "Unrestricted Net Position", "d": "This account is used to record the component of net position that represents net position not classified in accounts 760 and 770. This account is to be used only in proprietary funds and entity-wide statements. (This was previously fund balance code 760.)", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001353117414", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('FinancialExpenditureLevelofInstructionCode', 'This classification permits expenditures to be segregated by instructional level.', NULL, 'scheme: C001555', NULL, $j$[{"v": "10", "n": "Elementary", "d": "A school organization classified as elementary by state and local practice and composed of any span of grades from prekindergarten, kindergarten, or grade 1 through grade 8.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164554", "dep": null}, {"v": "11", "n": "Prekindergarten", "d": "A school organization composed entirely of any span of ages below kindergarten. This category is normally used for students identified as needing special services, although regular education prekindergarten would also be appropriate.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164555", "dep": null}, {"v": "12", "n": "Kindergarten", "d": "A school organization for children in the year immediately preceding first grade.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164556", "dep": null}, {"v": "19", "n": "Other Elementary", "d": "A school organization composed of any span of grades not above grade 8, except prekindergarten and kindergarten.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164557", "dep": null}, {"v": "20", "n": "Middle", "d": "A school organization composed of at least three grades, usually beginning with grade 4 through grade 6 or the equivalent and usually ending with grade 8 or grade 9. Most middle school organizations presume that students finishing middle school will go on to secondary school.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164558", "dep": null}, {"v": "30", "n": "Secondary", "d": "A school organization comprising any span of grades beginning with the next grade following an elementary or middle school, usually beginning with grade 7 through grade 10, and ending with or below grade 12.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164559", "dep": null}, {"v": "37", "n": "Elementary and Secondary Combined", "d": "A school organization comprising elementary and secondary levels of instruction, which may also include kindergarten and prekindergarten programs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164560", "dep": null}, {"v": "40", "n": "Postsecondary", "d": "A school organization providing formal instructional programs with a curriculum designed primarily for students who have completed the requirements for a high school diploma or the equivalent. This includes programs of an academic, vocational, and continuing professional education purpose and excludes avocational and adult education programs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164561", "dep": null}, {"v": "41", "n": "Programs for Adult/Continuing", "d": "A program for adults and out-of-school youth (typically 16 years of age and older who are not regularly enrolled in school) who have completed, interrupted, or not begun their formal education and are pursuing skills or knowledge in other than regularly prescribed courses. These include adult basic education programs and other programs for the pursuit of special interests or enrichment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164562", "dep": null}, {"v": "42", "n": "Community/Junior College", "d": "An institution of higher education that usually offers the first 2 years of college instruction and frequently grants an associate's degree, but does not grant a bachelor's degree. It is an independently organized institution (public or nonpublic), an institution that is part of a school district, or an independently organized system of junior colleges. Junior colleges offer college transfer courses and programs; vocational, technical, and semiprofessional occupational programs; or general education programs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164563", "dep": null}, {"v": "50", "n": "School Wide", "d": "For coding expenditures that cannot be clearly assigned to a specific instructional level.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164564", "dep": null}, {"v": "60", "n": "Early Learning Program", "d": "An organization classified as providing services during the stage in human development from birth through the early school years during which significant social, emotional, cognitive, language, psychological, and physical development occurs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001555164565", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('IndividualizedProgramType', 'A designation of the type of program developed for a student.', NULL, 'scheme: C000320', NULL, $j$[{"v": "02196", "n": "Individualized education program (IEP)", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is an individualized education program (IEP).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127903", "dep": null}, {"v": "02197", "n": "Individualized learning program (ILP)", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is an individualized learning program (ILP).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127904", "dep": null}, {"v": "02198", "n": "Individualized family service plan (IFSP)", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is an individualized family service plan (IFSP).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127905", "dep": null}, {"v": "02349", "n": "English learner", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is an English learner.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127906", "dep": null}, {"v": "05978", "n": "504 plan", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is a 504 plan.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127907", "dep": null}, {"v": "05979", "n": "Student intervention/support plan", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is a student intervention/support plan.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127908", "dep": null}, {"v": "05980", "n": "GIEP - Individualized education program for gifted student", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is a GIEP - Individualized education program for gifted student.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127909", "dep": null}, {"v": "05981", "n": "Literacy plan", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is a literacy plan.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127910", "dep": null}, {"v": "05982", "n": "Individualized transition plan", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is an individualized transition plan.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127911", "dep": null}, {"v": "09999", "n": "Other", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is in a category not yet defined in CEDS.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127912", "dep": null}, {"v": "89600", "n": "College and Career Ready Learning Plan", "d": "This type of individualized program developed for the student is a College and Career Ready Learning Plan.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320127913", "dep": null}, {"v": "75019", "n": "Behavior Intervention Plan (BIP)", "d": "The type of individualized program developed for the student is a Behavior Intervention Plan (BIP).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320190682", "dep": null}, {"v": "75020", "n": "Coordinated Early Intervening Services (CEIS)", "d": "The type of individualized program developed for the student is a coordinated early intervening service.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320928161", "dep": null}, {"v": "75021", "n": "Comprehensive Coordinated Early Intervening Services (CCEIS)", "d": "The type of individualized program developed for the student is a comprehensive coordinated early intervening service.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000320928162", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('LearnerActionType', 'The type of action taken by the learner.', NULL, 'scheme: C000934', NULL, $j$[{"v": "abandoned", "n": "Abandoned", "d": "Indicates the activity provider has determined that the session was abnormally terminated either by an actor or due to a system failure.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141309", "dep": null}, {"v": "answered", "n": "Answered", "d": "Indicates the actor replied to a question, where the object is generally an activity representing the question. The text of the answer will often be included in the response inside result.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141310", "dep": null}, {"v": "asked", "n": "Asked", "d": "Indicates an inquiry by an actor with the expectation of a response or answer to a question.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141311", "dep": null}, {"v": "attempted", "n": "Attempted", "d": "Indicates the actor made an effort to access the object. An attempt statement without additional activities could be considered incomplete in some cases.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141312", "dep": null}, {"v": "attended", "n": "Attended", "d": "Indicates the actor was present at a virtual or physical event or activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141313", "dep": null}, {"v": "commented", "n": "Commented", "d": "Indicates the actor provided digital or written annotations on or about an object.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141314", "dep": null}, {"v": "completed", "n": "Completed", "d": "Indicates the actor finished or concluded the activity normally.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141315", "dep": null}, {"v": "exited", "n": "Exited", "d": "Indicates the actor intentionally departed from the activity or object.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141316", "dep": null}, {"v": "experienced", "n": "Experienced", "d": "Indicates the actor only encountered the object, and is applicable in situations where a specific achievement or completion is not required.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141317", "dep": null}, {"v": "failed", "n": "Failed", "d": "Indicates the actor did not successfully pass an activity to a level of predetermined satisfaction.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141318", "dep": null}, {"v": "imported", "n": "Imported", "d": "Indicates the actor introduced an object into a physical or virtual location.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141319", "dep": null}, {"v": "initialized", "n": "Initialized", "d": "Indicates the activity provider has determined that the actor successfully started an activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141320", "dep": null}, {"v": "interacted", "n": "Interacted", "d": "Indicates the actor engaged with a physical or virtual object.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141321", "dep": null}, {"v": "launched", "n": "Launched", "d": "Indicates the actor attempted to start an activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141322", "dep": null}, {"v": "logged-in", "n": "Logged-In", "d": "Indicates the actor gained access to a system or service by identifying and authenticating with the credentials provided by the actor.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141323", "dep": null}, {"v": "logged-out", "n": "Logged-Out", "d": "Indicates the actor either lost or discontinued access to a system or service.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141324", "dep": null}, {"v": "mastered", "n": "Mastered", "d": "Indicates the highest level of comprehension or competence the actor performed in an activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141325", "dep": null}, {"v": "passed", "n": "Passed", "d": "Indicates the actor successfully passed an activity to a level of predetermined satisfaction.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141326", "dep": null}, {"v": "preferred", "n": "Preferred", "d": "Indicates the selected choices, favored options or settings of an actor in relation to an object or activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141327", "dep": null}, {"v": "progressed", "n": "Progressed", "d": "Indicates a value of how much of an actor has advanced or moved through an activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141328", "dep": null}, {"v": "registered", "n": "Registered", "d": "Indicates the actor is officially enrolled or inducted in an activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141329", "dep": null}, {"v": "responded", "n": "Responded", "d": "Indicates an actor reacted or replied to an object.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141330", "dep": null}, {"v": "resumed", "n": "Resumed", "d": "Indicates the application has determined that the actor continued or reopened a suspended attempt on an activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141331", "dep": null}, {"v": "satisfied", "n": "Satisfied", "d": "Indicates that the authority or activity provider determined the actor has fulfilled the criteria of the object or activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141332", "dep": null}, {"v": "scored", "n": "Scored", "d": "Indicates a numerical value related to an actor's performance on an activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141333", "dep": null}, {"v": "shared", "n": "Shared", "d": "Indicates the actor's intent to openly provide access to an object of common interest to other actors or groups.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141334", "dep": null}, {"v": "suspended", "n": "Suspended", "d": "Indicates the status of a temporarily halted activity when an actor's intent is returning to the or object activity at a later time.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141335", "dep": null}, {"v": "terminated", "n": "Terminated", "d": "Indicates that the actor successfully ended an activity.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141336", "dep": null}, {"v": "voided", "n": "Voided", "d": "A special reserved verb used by a LRS or application to mark a statement as invalid. See the xAPI specification for details on Voided statements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141337", "dep": null}, {"v": "waived", "n": "Waived", "d": "Indicates that the learning activity requirements were met by means other than completing the activity. A waived statement is used to indicate that the activity may be skipped by the actor.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000934141338", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('LearningResourceAccessRightsURL', 'A Uniform Resource Locator (URL) that identifies the conditions that govern the user''s ability to access a learning resource.', NULL, 'scheme: C001561', NULL, $j$[{"v": "FreeAccessWithRegistration", "n": "Free Access with Registration", "d": "The right to view and/or download material without financial barriers but users are required to register or experience some other low-barrier to use.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001561105862", "dep": null}, {"v": "LimitedFreeAccess", "n": "Limited Free Access", "d": "Some material is available for viewing and/or downloading but most material tends to be accessible through other means.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001561105863", "dep": null}, {"v": "AvailableForPurchase", "n": "Available for Purchase", "d": "The right to view, keep, and/or download material upon payment of a one-time fee.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001561105865", "dep": null}, {"v": "AvailableBySubscription", "n": "Available by Subscription", "d": "The right to view and/or download material, often for a set period of time, by way of a financial agreement between rights holders and authorized users.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001561105866", "dep": null}, {"v": "PublisherDefined", "n": "Publisher Defined", "d": "Publisher defined conditions that govern the user's ability to access a learning resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001561105867", "dep": null}, {"v": "FreeAccess", "n": "Free Access", "d": "The right to view and/or download material without financial, registration, or excessive advertising barriers.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001561106122", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('LearningResourceAuthorType', 'The type of entity, organization or person, that authored the learning resource.', NULL, 'scheme: C001562', NULL, $j$[{"v": "Organization", "n": "Organization", "d": "The specified author of the learning resource is an organization.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001562116337", "dep": null}, {"v": "Person", "n": "Person", "d": "The specified author of the learning resource is a person.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001562116536", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('LearningResourceInteractionMode', 'The primary type of interaction, synchronous or asynchronous, defined for the learning resource.', NULL, 'scheme: C001565', NULL, $j$[{"v": "Asynchronous", "n": "Student-oriented teaching and learning which is not organized around participants interacting at the same time and in the same space.", "d": "Student-oriented teaching and learning which is not organized around participants interacting at the same time and in the same space.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001565115301", "dep": null}, {"v": "Synchronous", "n": "Group-oriented teaching and learning organized around participants interacting at the same time and in the same space.", "d": "Group-oriented teaching and learning organized around participants interacting at the same time and in the same space.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001565116984", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('CompetencyAssociationType', 'Defines the nature of the association between a Competency Definition and an associated data object such as a Learning Resource, an Assessment Item, or even another Competency Definition.', NULL, 'scheme: C000869', NULL, $j$[{"v": "Assesses", "n": "Assesses", "d": "The origin of the association may be used to assess the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117229", "dep": null}, {"v": "ComplexityLevel", "n": "Complexity Level", "d": "The point in the framework being referenced defines a level or range that measures the difficulty or challenge presented by the learning resource being described.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117230", "dep": null}, {"v": "ConformsTo", "n": "Conforms To", "d": "The origin of the association conforms to an established standard that the destination defines.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117231", "dep": null}, {"v": "Defines", "n": "Defines", "d": "The information at origin of the association provides context or meaning for understanding the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117232", "dep": null}, {"v": "EducationalSubject", "n": "Educational Subject", "d": "The destination of the association defines a topic or subject from a controlled vocabulary.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117233", "dep": null}, {"v": "EducationLevel", "n": "Education Level", "d": "The destination of the association defines an education level from a controlled vocabulary.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117234", "dep": null}, {"v": "Follows", "n": "Follows", "d": "The origin of the association comes after the destination of the association in time or order.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117235", "dep": null}, {"v": "FormatOf", "n": "Is Format of", "d": "The destination of the association is substantially the same as the resource at the origin of the association, but in another format.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117236", "dep": null}, {"v": "HasFormat", "n": "Has Format", "d": "The destination of the association is substantially the same as the resource at the origin of the association, but in another format.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117237", "dep": null}, {"v": "HasPart", "n": "Has Part", "d": "The destination of the association is included either physically or logically in the resource at the origin of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117238", "dep": null}, {"v": "HasVersion", "n": "Has Version", "d": "The destination of the association is a version, edition, or adaptation of the resource at the origin of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117239", "dep": null}, {"v": "IsAssessedBy", "n": "Is Assessed By", "d": "The destination of the association may be used to assess the origin of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117240", "dep": null}, {"v": "IsConcurrentTo", "n": "Is Concurrent To", "d": "The origin of the association is achieved or delivered at the same time, or has the same ordinal position, as the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117241", "dep": null}, {"v": "IsConformedTo", "n": "Is Conformed To", "d": "The destination of the association references an established standard to which the origin of the association conforms.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117242", "dep": null}, {"v": "IsDefinedBy", "n": "Is Defined By", "d": "Context or meaning for understanding the origin of the association is provided by the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117243", "dep": null}, {"v": "IsPartOf", "n": "Is Part Of", "d": "The origin of the association is included either physically or logically in the resource at the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117244", "dep": null}, {"v": "IsPrerequisiteTo", "n": "Is Prerequisite To", "d": "The origin of the association is required as a prior condition for the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117245", "dep": null}, {"v": "IsTaughtBy", "n": "Is Taught By", "d": "The competency at the origin of the association may be taught by the resource or method at the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117246", "dep": null}, {"v": "Precedes", "n": "Precedes", "d": "The origin of the association comes before the destination of the association in time or order.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117247", "dep": null}, {"v": "Prerequisite", "n": "Prerequisite", "d": "The destination of the association is required as a prior condition for the origin of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117248", "dep": null}, {"v": "ReadingLevel", "n": "Reading Level", "d": "The destination of the association defines a level or range of ability expected for a person using the resource at the origin of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117249", "dep": null}, {"v": "Referenced", "n": "Referenced", "d": "The origin of the association cites the resource at the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117250", "dep": null}, {"v": "ReferencedBy", "n": "Is Referenced By", "d": "The origin of the association is cited by the resource at the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117251", "dep": null}, {"v": "ReplacedBy", "n": "Is Replaced By", "d": "The origin of the association has been supplanted by, displaced by, or superseded by the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117252", "dep": null}, {"v": "RequiredBy", "n": "Is Required By", "d": "The origin of the association is required by the destination of the association to support its function, delivery, or coherence.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117253", "dep": null}, {"v": "Requires", "n": "Requires", "d": "The origin of the association requires the destination of the association to support its function, delivery, or coherence.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117254", "dep": null}, {"v": "Teaches", "n": "Teaches", "d": "The resource or method at the origin of the association may be used to teach the competency at the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117255", "dep": null}, {"v": "VersionOf", "n": "Is Version Of", "d": "The origin of the association is a version, edition, or adaptation of the resource at the destination of the association.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000869117256", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
