 "notes": "concept: NI000540116486", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('NAEPMathematicalComplexityLevel', 'Complexity levels defined by the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP 2005a Framework).', NULL, 'scheme: C001088', NULL, $j$[{"v": "LowComplexity", "n": "Low complexity", "d": "This category relies heavily on the recall and recognition of previously learned concepts and principles. Items typically specify what the student is to do, which is often to carry out some procedure that can be performed mechanically. It is not left to the student to come up with an original method or solution.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001088104244", "dep": null}, {"v": "ModerateComplexity", "n": "Moderate complexity", "d": "Items in the moderate-complexity category involve more flexibility of thinking and choice among alternatives than do those in the low-complexity category. They require a response that goes beyond the habitual, is not specified, and ordinarily has more than a single step. The student is expected to decide what to do, using informal methods of reasoning and problem-solving strategies, and to bring together skill and knowledge from various domains.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001088104245", "dep": null}, {"v": "HighComplexity", "n": "High complexity", "d": "High-complexity items make heavy demands on students, who must engage in more abstract reasoning, planning, analysis, judgment, and creative thought. A satisfactory response to the item requires that the student think in an abstract and sophisticated way.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001088104246", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('AssessmentItemTextComplexitySystem', 'The scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.', NULL, 'scheme: C000907', NULL, $j$[{"v": "01", "n": "Automated Readability Index", "d": "Automated Readability Index is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907113589", "dep": null}, {"v": "02", "n": "Bormuth Index", "d": "Bormuth Index is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907113766", "dep": null}, {"v": "03", "n": "Coleman Liau Index", "d": "Coleman Liau Index is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907113877", "dep": null}, {"v": "04", "n": "Coh-Metrix Readability", "d": "Coh-Metrix Readability is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114081", "dep": null}, {"v": "05", "n": "Dale-Chall Readability Formula", "d": "Dale-Chall Readability Formula is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114207", "dep": null}, {"v": "06", "n": "Flesch-Kincaid Grade Level", "d": "Flesch-Kincaid Grade Level is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114253", "dep": null}, {"v": "07", "n": "Flesch Reading Ease Formula", "d": "Flesch Reading Ease Formula is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114290", "dep": null}, {"v": "08", "n": "FORCAST", "d": "FORCAST is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114312", "dep": null}, {"v": "09", "n": "Fry Readability Formula", "d": "Fry Readability Formula is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114330", "dep": null}, {"v": "10", "n": "Gunning-Fog Scale", "d": "Gunning-Fog Scale is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114388", "dep": null}, {"v": "11", "n": "Hull Formula", "d": "Hull Formula is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114415", "dep": null}, {"v": "12", "n": "Lexile", "d": "Lexile is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114438", "dep": null}, {"v": "13", "n": "Linsear Write Formula", "d": "Linsear Write Formula is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114465", "dep": null}, {"v": "14", "n": "McAlpine EFLAW", "d": "McAlpine EFLAW is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114606", "dep": null}, {"v": "15", "n": "Powers-Sumner-Kearl", "d": "Powers-Sumner-Kearl is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114625", "dep": null}, {"v": "16", "n": "Raygor Readability Estimate", "d": "Raygor Readability Estimate is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114647", "dep": null}, {"v": "17", "n": "SMOG Index", "d": "SMOG Index is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114662", "dep": null}, {"v": "18", "n": "Spache Readability Formula", "d": "Spache Readability Formula is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114675", "dep": null}, {"v": "19", "n": "Strain Index", "d": "Strain Index is specified as the scaling system used to specify the text complexity of an assessment item.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000907114681", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('AssessmentItemInteractionType', 'The assessment item body interaction type as defined by IMS Global specifications.', NULL, 'scheme: C001158', NULL, $j$[{"v": "CustomInteraction", "n": "Custom Interaction", "d": "The custom interaction provides an opportunity for extensibility of this specification to include support for interactions not currently documented.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104266", "dep": null}, {"v": "DrawingInteraction", "n": "Drawing Interaction", "d": "The drawing interaction allows the candidate to use a common set of drawing tools to modify a given graphical image (the canvas). It must be bound to a response variable with base-type file and single cardinality. The result is a file in the same format as the original image.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104267", "dep": null}, {"v": "GapMatchInteraction", "n": "Gap Match Interaction", "d": "A gap match interaction contains a number gaps that the candidate can fill from an associated set of choices. The candidate must be able to review the content with the gaps filled in context, as indicated by their choices.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104268", "dep": null}, {"v": "MatchInteraction", "n": "Match Interaction", "d": "A match interaction presents candidates with two sets of choices and allows them to create associates between pairs of choices in the two sets, but not between pairs of choices in the same set. Further restrictions can still be placed on the allowable associations using the matchMax attribute of the choices.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104269", "dep": null}, {"v": "GraphicGapMatchInteraction", "n": "Graphic Gap Match Interaction", "d": "A graphic gap-match interaction is a graphical interaction with a set of gaps that are defined as areas (hotspots) of the graphic image and an additional set of gap choices that are defined outside the image. The candidate must associate the gap choices with the gaps in the image and be able to review the image with the gaps filled in context, as indicated by their choices. Care should be taken when designing these interactions to ensure that the gaps in the image are a suitable size to receive the required gap choices. It must be clear to the candidate which hotspot each choice has been associated with. When associated, choices must appear wholly inside the gaps if at all possible and, where overlaps are required, should not hide each other completely. If the candidate indicates the association by positioning the choice over the gap (e.g., drag and drop) the system should 'snap' it to the nearest position that satisfies these requirements.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104270", "dep": null}, {"v": "HotspotInteraction", "n": "Hotspot Interaction", "d": "A hotspot interaction is a graphical interaction with a corresponding set of choices that are defined as areas of the graphic image. The candidate's task is to select one or more of the areas (hotspots). The hotspot interaction should only be used when the spatial relationship of the choices with respect to each other (as represented by the graphic image) is important to the needs of the item. Otherwise, choiceInteraction should be used instead with separate material for each option.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104271", "dep": null}, {"v": "GraphicOrderInteraction", "n": "Graphic Order Interaction", "d": "A graphic order interaction is a graphic interaction with a corresponding set of choices that are defined as areas of the graphic image. The candidate's task is to impose an ordering on the areas (hotspots). The order hotspot interaction should only be used when the spatial relationship of the choices with respect to each other (as represented by the graphic image) is important to the needs of the item. Otherwise, orderInteraction should be used instead with separate material for each option.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104272", "dep": null}, {"v": "OrderInteraction", "n": "Order Interaction", "d": "In an order interaction the candidate's task is to reorder the choices, the order in which the choices are displayed initially is significant. By default the candidate's task is to order all of the choices but a subset of the choices can be requested using the maxChoices and minChoices attributes. When specified the candidate must select a subset of the choices and impose an ordering on them.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104279", "dep": null}, {"v": "GraphicAssociateInteraction", "n": "Graphic Associate Interaction", "d": "A graphic associate interaction is a graphic interaction with a corresponding set of choices that are defined as areas of the graphic image. The candidate's task is to associate the areas (hotspots) with each other. The graphic associate interaction should only be used when the graphical relationship of the choices with respect to each other (as represented by the graphic image) is important to the needs of the item. Otherwise, associateInteraction should be used instead with separate Material for each option. SliderInteraction -- The slider interaction presents the candidate with a control for selecting a numerical value between a lower and upper bound. It must be bound to a response variable with single cardinality with a base-type of either integer or float.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104274", "dep": null}, {"v": "ChoiceInteraction", "n": "Choice Interaction", "d": "The choice interaction presents a set of choices to the candidate. The candidate's task is to select one or more of the choices, up to a maximum of maxChoices. The interaction is always initialized with no choices selected.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104275", "dep": null}, {"v": "InlineChoiceInteraction", "n": "Inline Choice Interaction", "d": "A inline choice is an inlineInteraction that presents the user with a set of choices, each of which is a simple piece of text. The candidate's task is to select one of the choices. Unlike the choiceInteraction, the delivery engine must allow the candidate to review their choice within the context of the surrounding text.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104276", "dep": null}, {"v": "MediaInteraction", "n": "Media Interaction", "d": "The media interaction allows more control over the way the candidate interacts with a time-based media object and allows the number of times the media object was experienced to be reported in the value of the associated response variable, which must be of base-type integer and single cardinality.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104277", "dep": null}, {"v": "HottextInteraction", "n": "Hottext Interaction", "d": "The hottext interaction presents a set of choices to the candidate represented as selectable runs of text embedded within a surrounding context, such as a simple passage of text. Like choiceInteraction, the candidate's task is to select one or more of the choices, up to a maximum of maxChoices. The interaction is initialized from the defaultValue of the associated response variable, a NULL value indicating that no choices are selected (the usual case).", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104278", "dep": null}, {"v": "PositionObjectInteraction", "n": "Position Object Interaction", "d": "The position object interaction consists of a single image which must be positioned on another graphic image (the stage) by the candidate. Like selectPointInteraction, the associated response may have an areaMapping that scores the response on the basis of comparing it against predefined areas but the delivery engine must not indicate these areas of the stage. Only the actual position(s) selected by the candidate shall be indicated.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104280", "dep": null}, {"v": "TextEntryInteraction", "n": "Text Entry Interaction", "d": "A textEntry interaction obtains a simple piece of text from the candidate. Like inlineChoiceInteraction, the delivery engine must allow the candidate to review their choice within the context of the surrounding text.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104281", "dep": null}, {"v": "ExtendedTextInteraction", "n": "Extended Text Interaction", "d": "An extended text interaction allows the candidate to enter an extended amount of text.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104282", "dep": null}, {"v": "EndAttemptInteraction", "n": "End Attempt Interaction", "d": "The end attempt interaction is a special type of interaction which allows item authors to provide the candidate with control over the way in which the candidate terminates an attempt. The candidate can use the interaction to terminate the attempt (triggering response processing) immediately, typically to request a hint. It must be bound to a response variable with base-type boolean and single cardinality.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104283", "dep": null}, {"v": "UploadInteraction", "n": "Upload Interaction", "d": "The upload interaction allows the candidate to upload a pre-prepared file representing their response. It must be bound to a response variable with base-type file and single cardinality.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104284", "dep": null}, {"v": "AssociateInteraction", "n": "Associate Interaction", "d": "An associate interaction presents candidates with a number of choices and allows them to create associations between them.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001158104285", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('IdentificationSystemForAssessmentFormSection', 'A coding scheme that is used for identification of an Assessment Form Section.', NULL, 'scheme: C001190', NULL, $j$[{"v": "Client", "n": "Client", "d": "The related Assessment Form Section Identifier is based on the identification system defined by the Client.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001190115436", "dep": null}, {"v": "Internal", "n": "Internal", "d": "The related Assessment Form Section Identifier is based on the identification system defined internally.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001190115955", "dep": null}, {"v": "Other", "n": "Other", "d": "The related Assessment Form Section Identifier is based on an identification system in a category not yet defined in CEDS.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001190116405", "dep": null}, {"v": "Publisher", "n": "Publisher", "d": "The related Assessment Form Section Identifier is based on the identification system defined by the Publisher.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001190116660", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('AssessmentAssetType', 'Specifies a predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource. Assessment assets represent any content used to compose an assessment item, is referenced by an item but not part of the item content itself, or is content that is included as part of a section within an assessment form. Assets can be static content such as art work or dynamic assets such as calculators.', NULL, 'scheme: C001196', NULL, $j$[{"v": "Audio", "n": "Audio", "d": "Audio is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196115314", "dep": null}, {"v": "BasicCalculator", "n": "Basic calculator", "d": "Basic calculator is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196115343", "dep": null}, {"v": "Chart", "n": "Chart", "d": "Chart is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196115419", "dep": null}, {"v": "EnglishRuler", "n": "English ruler", "d": "English ruler is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196115652", "dep": null}, {"v": "FormulaSheet", "n": "Formula sheet", "d": "Formula sheet is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196115760", "dep": null}, {"v": "GraphicArt", "n": "Graphic art", "d": "Graphic art is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196115815", "dep": null}, {"v": "GraphingCalculator", "n": "Graphing calculator", "d": "Graphing calculator is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196115817", "dep": null}, {"v": "Highlighter", "n": "Highlighter", "d": "Highlighter is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196115852", "dep": null}, {"v": "LabSet", "n": "Lab set", "d": "Lab set is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116000", "dep": null}, {"v": "LineDraw", "n": "Line draw", "d": "Line draw is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116037", "dep": null}, {"v": "Map", "n": "Map", "d": "Map is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116071", "dep": null}, {"v": "MetricRuler", "n": "Metric ruler", "d": "Metric ruler is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116109", "dep": null}, {"v": "Other", "n": "Other", "d": "Other is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116366", "dep": null}, {"v": "OtherInteractive", "n": "Other interactive", "d": "Other interactive is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116449", "dep": null}, {"v": "OtherNonInteractive", "n": "Other non-interactive", "d": "Other non-interactive is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116454", "dep": null}, {"v": "PeriodicTable", "n": "Periodic table", "d": "Periodic table is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116528", "dep": null}, {"v": "Protractor", "n": "Protractor", "d": "Protractor is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116640", "dep": null}, {"v": "ReadingLine", "n": "Reading line", "d": "Reading line is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116691", "dep": null}, {"v": "ReadingPassage", "n": "Reading passage", "d": "Reading passage is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116692", "dep": null}, {"v": "Scenario", "n": "Scenario", "d": "Scenario is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116794", "dep": null}, {"v": "ScientificCalculator", "n": "Scientific calculator", "d": "Scientific calculator is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116816", "dep": null}, {"v": "Simulation", "n": "Simulation", "d": "Simulation is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116864", "dep": null}, {"v": "StandardCalculator", "n": "Standard calculator", "d": "Standard calculator is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116920", "dep": null}, {"v": "StoryBoard", "n": "Story board", "d": "Story board is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116958", "dep": null}, {"v": "Table", "n": "Table", "d": "Table is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196116987", "dep": null}, {"v": "TranslationDictionary", "n": "Translation dictionary", "d": "Translation dictionary is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196117079", "dep": null}, {"v": "UnitsRuler", "n": "Units ruler", "d": "Units ruler is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196117115", "dep": null}, {"v": "Video", "n": "Video", "d": "Video is specified as the predominant type of assessment asset represented by the Learning Resource.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001196117151", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('AssessmentAssetIdentifierType', 'The type of identifier that is provided for this asset.', NULL, 'scheme: C001199', NULL, $j$[{"v": "Client", "n": "Assigned by the client", "d": "Assigned by the client is specified as the type of identifier that is provided for this assessment asset.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001199115434", "dep": null}, {"v": "Internal", "n": "Provided by an internal assessment service", "d": "Provided by an internal assessment serviced is specified as the type of identifier that is provided for this assessment asset.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001199115956", "dep": null}, {"v": "Other", "n": "Custom identifier", "d": "Custom identifier is specified as the type of identifier that is provided for this assessment asset.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001199116343", "dep": null}, {"v": "Publisher", "n": "Assigned by the asset owner", "d": "Assigned by the asset owner is specified as the type of identifier that is provided for this assessment asset.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001199116658", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('NAEPAspectsOfReading', 'Aspects of reading defined by the National Assessment of Educational Progress (NAEP 2005b Framework).', NULL, 'scheme: C001122', NULL, $j$[{"v": "DevelopingInterpretation", "n": "Developing Interpretation", "d": "To develop an interpretation, the reader must extend initial impressions to arrive at a more complete understanding of what was read. This involves linking information across parts of a text as well as focusing on specific information.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001122104350", "dep": null}, {"v": "MakingReaderTextConnections", "n": "Making reader/text connections", "d": "To make reader/text connections, the reader must link information in the text with knowledge and experience. This might include applying ideas in the text to the real world, and responses must be text based.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001122104351", "dep": null}, {"v": "ExaminingContentAndStructure", "n": "Examining content and structure", "d": "Examining text content and structure requires critically evaluating, comparing and contrasting, and understanding the effect of features such as irony, humor, and organization. Readers are required to stand apart from the text, consider it objectively, and evaluate its quality and appropriateness, using text content and structure.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001122104352", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('ClassroomPositionType', 'The type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.', NULL, 'scheme: C000622', NULL, $j$[{"v": "00059", "n": "Paraprofessionals/teacher aides", "d": "Paraprofessionals/teacher aides is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622113418", "dep": null}, {"v": "00069", "n": "Non-instructional staff", "d": "Non-instructional staff is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622113424", "dep": null}, {"v": "00080", "n": "Student teachers", "d": "Student teachers is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622113425", "dep": null}, {"v": "01234", "n": "Intern", "d": "Intern is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622113663", "dep": null}, {"v": "01382", "n": "Volunteer/no contract", "d": "Volunteer/no contract is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622113679", "dep": null}, {"v": "03187", "n": "Administrative staff", "d": "Administrative staff is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622113994", "dep": null}, {"v": "04725", "n": "Counselor", "d": "Counselor is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622114149", "dep": null}, {"v": "04735", "n": "Resource teacher", "d": "Resource teacher is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622114163", "dep": null}, {"v": "05971", "n": "Primary instructor", "d": "Primary instructor is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622114235", "dep": null}, {"v": "05972", "n": "Secondary instructor", "d": "Secondary instructor is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622114236", "dep": null}, {"v": "05973", "n": "Instructor of record", "d": "Instructor of record is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622114237", "dep": null}, {"v": "09999", "n": "Other", "d": "Other is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622114363", "dep": null}, {"v": "73071", "n": "Co-teacher", "d": "Co-teacher is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622115060", "dep": null}, {"v": "73072", "n": "Lead Team Teacher", "d": "Lead Team Teacher is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622115061", "dep": null}, {"v": "73073", "n": "Course Proctor", "d": "Course Proctor is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622115062", "dep": null}, {"v": "73074", "n": "Special Education Consultant", "d": "Special Education Consultant is specified as the type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI000622115063", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
SELECT public.ceds_tmp_valueset('CourseSectionInstructionalDeliveryMode', 'The primary setting or medium of delivery for the course.', NULL, 'scheme: C001161', NULL, $j$[{"v": "Broadcast", "n": "Broadcast", "d": "Course is taught via live or taped broadcast over open air, closed circuit, or cable television systems.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001161104363", "dep": null}, {"v": "Correspondence", "n": "Correspondence", "d": "Course is taught via hard or electronic copy or other media (CD, DVD, video cassette) and student works at own pace usually without an instructor present, but generally under supervision of LEA. Includes \"packet\" programs.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001161104364", "dep": null}, {"v": "EarlyCollege", "n": "Early College", "d": "Course is taught by institution of higher education, but does NOT qualify as concurrent enrollment.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001161104365", "dep": null}, {"v": "AudioVideo", "n": "Interactive Audio/Video", "d": "Course is taught via remote interactive receiver or via streaming media technologies.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001161104366", "dep": null}, {"v": "Online", "n": "Online", "d": "Course is taught through a website, web application, or app on an internet connected device.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001161104367", "dep": null}, {"v": "IndependentStudy", "n": "Independent Study", "d": "Structured learning experience is recognized for credit but is not under supervision of the LEA.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001161104368", "dep": null}, {"v": "FaceToFace", "n": "Face to Face", "d": "Course is taught primarily in person and usually in a conventional classroom or lecture hall.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001161104369", "dep": null}, {"v": "BlendedLearning", "n": "Blended Learning", "d": "Course uses a blended learning model that includes Face to Face and Online components.", "u": null, "notes": "concept: NI001161104370", "dep": null}]$j$::jsonb);
